# UI taste (WiChat product)

When **designing, redesigning, polishing, or reviewing** WiChat web UI (shell, chat, auth chrome), read and follow:

**[.agents/skills/design-taste-frontend/SKILL.md](../../.agents/skills/design-taste-frontend/SKILL.md)** — tasteskill 2.5 (anti-slop).

## WiChat adaptation (not a marketing page)

| tasteskill default | WiChat |
| --- | --- |
| Static landing + `gate.mjs` rounds | **Skip gate** for `apps/web` routes; use manual browser check + `pnpm lint` / typecheck |
| Hero / photo chapters | **Product shell** — sidebar, rail, header, composer, empty states |
| Shader scenes | **No** WebGL in core chat shell v1 |
| site-kind place / cafe | **site-kind software** — real app UI, tokens in `globals.css` |

## Apply in-app

- **One system:** reuse `--shell-rail-*`, `--chat-*`, sidebar tokens; no one-off hex unless tokenized.
- **Quiet motion (rule 5):** hover/press on tiles and composer actions; respect `motion-reduce`; no gratuitous parallax or scroll-linked card motion.
- **Real product UI:** show actual WiChat surfaces in mocks/screenshots, not generic dashboard filler.
- **Copy:** i18n keys only (`packages/i18n`); plain, specific strings — no lorem or “AI” filler.
- **Equal edges:** message gutter (`max-w-[60rem]`) aligned with composer; shell chrome consistent with `wichat-web-layout.mdc`.

## Shell rail motion (when touching rail open/close)

- Current: `transition-[width]` on column + border-radius on main pane (~280ms). Acceptable for ~64px rail; **layout reflow** each frame is the main cost, not GPU shaders.
- **Revamp only if jank is measured:** prefer `transform` + fixed rail width + `overflow: hidden` over animating `width`; avoid stacking heavy work (large lists re-layout) during toggle; keep `motion-reduce:transition-none`.

## Order of reads

1. This rule + `wichat-web-layout.mdc` / `wichat-web-data.mdc`
2. `design-taste-frontend/SKILL.md` (house rules + software row in §1–2)
3. Implement; verify in browser at lg + mobile widths.
